  "reason": "Evidence: config_007 (scgpt + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted) achieved the best accuracy (0.542) at a lower cost (2.94 GPU hrs) than config_008 (scgpt + resnet50 + avgpool + weighted, 0.525 acc, 4.42 GPU hrs), suggesting the ViT-L image encoder is the stronger backbone. Uncertainty: we have only tested one fusion strategy (weighted) and one aggregation (avgpool), so it is unclear whether concat fusion could further improve on the best result. Question tested: config_016 changes only the fusion from weighted to concat while keeping the best-performing backbone (scgpt + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool), directly isolating the fusion effect. Why this is the best next experiment: it is a minimal, cheap (~3 GPU hrs, comparable to config_007) exploitation of the current best direction, reducing uncertainty about fusion before committing to larger architectural changes (transformer aggregation, different RNA encoders, or singleprofile). With 7 experiments remaining, establishing the optimal fusion for the best backbone early allows subsequent experiments to build on a stronger foundation."
